  "body": "### What is the issue with the URL Pattern Standard?\n\nFrom what I understand, the following WPT test: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/11d0a493dc7f9552ce1f99da80bb6e9238a60510/urlpattern/resources/urlpatterntestdata.json#L1235\n\nFails on a spec conforming implementation. This is because the basic URL parser with state override as 'port state' does not fail in: [\"canonicalize a port\"](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-a-port).\n\nIt instead sets the port to \"null\" and returns due to the following sequence:\n\n * Step 1 of port state: code point of 'I' is not an ASCII digit\n *  Step 2 of port state: state override is provided\n * Step 2.1 of port state: buffer is the empty string\n * Step 2.2 of port state: state override is given, so URL parser returns.\n\n\nAs an idea of a potential fix, step 2.2 of port state parser in URL spec could be changed to return failure if code point is not EOF.\n\ncc @annevk ",
